BlockyEngine -- notices
=======================

These notes used to sit at the bottom of LICENSE. They were moved here because
appending anything to the licence text stops GitHub recognising the file as
MIT: it reported the repository as NOASSERTION, which is a worse answer than
either the licence or the notes deserve. LICENSE is now the MIT text and
nothing else; what it does not say lives here.

The licence covers the source in this repository and nothing else.


Minecraft
---------

BlockyEngine is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to Mojang
Studios or Microsoft. "Minecraft" is a trademark of Mojang Studios.

The engine ships no game assets and requires none. Block textures are generated
in code, characters are drawn in code, and the built-in font is its own. What
it can do is *read* an installation you already have -- a client .jar or a
resource pack -- and some of the images under docs/gallery/ were rendered that
way. Those images show textures belonging to their respective owners, are
included to demonstrate the reader rather than to redistribute the artwork, and
are marked as such in the gallery. Nothing under engine/, game/ or scenes/
contains any of it.


Third-party code
----------------

There is none. Every line under engine/, game/ and scenes/ was written for this
project: the PNG codec, the ZIP reader, the OpenGL loader, the window, the
maths, the physics solver, the scripting language and the H.264 encoder
included. The only libraries linked are opengl32, user32 and gdi32, which ship
with Windows.

CONTRIBUTING.md says the same thing as a rule rather than as a fact, because it
is the one that has to hold going forward.
